AB  - Small-scale designer brands typically have a single designer leading the accomplishments of the brand. Thus, the individuality of the designer, encompassing their interests and direction of attention, is a very important issue in understanding the brand. Resultantly, this study focused on this individuality, a differentiating element of designer brands developing in the Korean domestic fashion industry. Empirical research was used to analyze (1) how designers express their individuality through brand individuality and (2) how consumers perceive designers’ individuality expressed through their brands. Specifically, this study utilized literary research and content analysis, as well as the qualitative technique of ethnography research. This author sought and presented detailed strategies to express the individuality of designers to improve their respective business operations. Therefore, this study is meaningful because it focused on the novel approach of considering designers and their individuality in an attempt to deepen the understanding of their brands.
