AB  - Minimalist fashion is becoming a more common choice for consumers in consideration of individual values and responsibility for the environment. Therefore, the purpose of this study was to take “minimalist fashion” as the research subject and to use text-mining analysis and content analysis to determine the detailed characteristics of minimalist fashion on social media and its implementation methods and effects. The specific research results were as follows. First, as a result of the analysis of the frequency of keywords related to minimalist fashion, “dress” appeared the most (53 times). Second, “minimalist capsule wardrobe” accounted for an overwhelming proportion of the analysis results of terms similar to minimalist fashion in the titles of the videos. Third, in the analysis results of the noteworthy implementation methods and effects in relation to minimalist fashion revealed three types of implementation methods (“composition of capsule wardrobe,” “creation of personal style,” and “wish list creation and value consumption”) and three types of implementation effects (“economic,” “convenience and satisfaction” and “creative”).
